<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need downtime?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If you validate behind a temporary hostname and lower TTL, downtime is often a few minutes or less."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if something breaks after cutover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Roll back DNS to the old target and troubleshoot with logs and health checks, then retry the cutover."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>


<h1 id="primary-question">How do I migrate a website to AWS with near‑zero downtime?</h1>
<p class="answer lead">Stage the target environment, import and validate the site behind a temporary hostname, lower DNS TTL to ~300 seconds, then switch records during a low‑traffic window. Monitor logs and performance; roll back if errors spike. Practice the steps ahead of time to make the cutover routine.</p>
